  "body": {
    "id": "thm:ordinary-id-reduction",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "If \\(H=\\{s_\\emptyset\\}\\), every selector gate is laid back on \\(E_H\\), and \\(S\\) has no latent root shared with \\(V\\), then, after suppressing the deterministic selector coordinate while retaining its provenance record, \\(G_H^N\\) has exactly the ordinary semi-Markovian recursive equations on \\(V\\), and \\(\\Phi_H\\) equals the ordinary observational-target relation.  Selector-correction transitions are vacuous, while every admitted reachable-fixing and labelled-elimination transition is algebraically the corresponding ordinary CADMG operation.  This reduction does not by itself assert that the frozen residual candidate libraries realize the complete ID formula-or-hedge classification.",
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:normalization-equivalence",
      "def:selector-transition",
      "def:fixing-transition",
      "def:elimination-transition",
      "def:sa-csid-machine"
    ],
    "justification": "The reduction is the required sanity check that the new calculus agrees with classical completeness when systematic selection disappears.",
    "gap": "Classical ID supplies the known endpoint, while the new work must show that the support-aware state and certificate semantics collapse to it exactly.",
    "consumer": "Implementers can regression-test the new backend against established ID outputs on ordinary hidden-variable DAGs.",
    "proof_tex": "Exact support \\(H=\\{s_\\emptyset\\}\\) implies \\(P(S=s_\\emptyset)=1\\).  Since every gate is laid back at that value, the known multiplexer selects the natural structural equation at each substantive node.  The absence of a latent root shared by \\(S\\) and \\(V\\) ensures that suppressing the now deterministic selector coordinate does not remove a substantive common cause.  The retained normalization deletes only the constant gate arguments and keeps every natural response table and latent-root law.  Consequently its substantive recursive equations are precisely those of the ordinary semi-Markovian expansion on \\(V\\).\n\nFor every \\(v\\),\n\\[\np_\\theta(V=v,S=s_\\emptyset)=p_\\theta(V=v),\n\\]\nand intervention at \\(S=s_\\emptyset\\) changes no laid-back gate.  Normalization equivalence therefore identifies \\(\\Phi_H\\), after omission of the constant selector coordinate, with the ordinary pair consisting of the observational law of \\(V\\) and the intervention \\(do(A=a)\\) target.\n\nThere is no active selector override, so \\(\\Sigma\\) is empty and selector correction is vacuous.  The reachability predicate in \\(\\textnormal{def:fixing-transition}\\) is the ordinary CADMG predicate \\(\\operatorname{dis}_D(W)\\cap\\operatorname{de}_D(W)=\\{W\\}\\), and its kernel quotient is the ordinary fixing quotient.  The two cases in \\(\\textnormal{def:elimination-transition}\\) are ordinary marginalization and proper-district factorization.  Hence every admitted nonresidual transition agrees algebraically with its ordinary counterpart.  Nothing in these observations forces the finite residual lists \\(\\mathcal P\\) and \\(\\mathcal C\\) to contain a standard hedge certificate, so the stronger classification claim does not follow.",
